From 20adc839bd036885679b0f82d258a381214bf842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:15:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Quit ~650 ms sooner on the RG DS Plus: the sound
 device's last close left to an exec'd helper; DSFLIP_LOG_TIME

DraStic is SIGKILLed to quit; its last thread to exit closed the output PCM, and the aw88166 amplifiers' stop (DSP
writes over I2C) held that exit ~600 ms, then the DRM release ~90 ms: superdrastic-run's wait, and so the menu,
waited for it. Before each quit's SIGKILL (resume.c quit_kill), audio_hand_off forks a helper that keeps only the
output's file (dup'd to fd 3) and execs /bin/sh with an empty environment, polling /proc/<drastic> every 50 ms; the
close then happens in the helper's exit. Exec'd at once, it holds none of DraStic's memory or display mappings
(0.4.2's fork-only try kept them; HYPOTHESIS: that was its 'display busy' next start). Async-signal-safe (the USR1
handler calls it). DSFLIP_AUDIO_CLOSE_CHILD=0 turns it off.

DSFLIP_LOG_TIME=1: log lines prefixed with CLOCK_BOOTTIME (LOG() now goes through dsflip_log), and a
'[start] first frame committed' mark.

RG DS Plus, Mario Kart DS, exit combo -> menu picture, alternated: stock 1465/1469 ms, this 879/773 ms; the next
start after each hand-off quit was normal (no 'display busy', no passthrough).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 365f5c9e835aea1fb59d5f77861e86e777819099)

ROCKNIXDS (agiacalone fork) conflict notes: our resume.c's quit logic
(stall watch, repeat handling, quit_watch) is kept; its SIGKILLs on the
quit paths go through quit_kill. The exit combo's direct quit_kill when
quit_saves is off is left out (no quit_saves on our line). The audio
hand-off is OFF unless DSFLIP_AUDIO_CLOSE_CHILD=1: on ROCKNIX the
output's poll file is PipeWire's socket, not the amplifiers' device.
