From ee81b2ca7b1c3541d80883aad03ce397146c10ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:49:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] low latency: DraStic no longer held to start late by
 default (DSFLIP_LOWLAT_ALIGN=1 to have it), and why

The hold (lowlat_hold) was cut short by DraStic's sound in nearly every frame: DraStic keeps only ~25 ms of
sound ahead of the pump at its present (15 ms at least: the pump's ring holds the rest), the hold wanted 13-19 ms
on average and the sound's floor is 8-25 ms ("let go early" 590-600 of 600 per 10 s in every run). Cut short, the
frame came after its deadline anyway (250-400 of 600 "held to the next"), waited a refresh more, and the next hold
aimed past that one: drops and hitches. Off by default now; the [lowlat] 10 s line gains DraStic's sound at its
present, the floor and the hold wanted, to look at it again.

RG DS, Mario Kart DS (QA's cold-start route: A taps through the menus into a race), DSFLIP_LOWLAT=1, 60 s held:
  before (4 runs): hitch seconds (a flip gap > 25 ms) 13 / 1 / 29 / 8, drops after the start 28 / 4 / 90 / 26
  after (3 runs):  hitch seconds 0 / 1 / 0, drops 0 / 0 / 0 (DSFLIP_LOWLAT=0: 0 and 0)
  present -> screen 22-28 ms before, 25-30 after (off: 53)
RG DS, Golden Sun: Dark Dawn intro: hitch 2, drops 4 -> 0, 0; present -> screen 25.9 -> 24.9 ms.
RG DS Plus: no change either way (hitch seconds 11-19 before, 16-17 after; off 10): DraStic runs 60.0 frames a
second against the Plus's 60.17 Hz panels, and its frames come bunched; low latency there stays rougher than off.

